(3) The Council shall have the power to do all things expedient or reasonably necessary for or incidental to the carrying out of its functions.

(4) The Council shall be responsible to the Minister and the Minister may give the Council directions of a general character, not inconsistent with the provisions of this Order, and the Council shall give effect to such directions.

